[ ] Make add honor --workspace as an exact write target =add-workspace-target $On add, --workspace should name the write target exactly. Today it is ignored or matched by substring; instead it should error when it names no workspace or more than one. Check add charter and add plan as well.$ !2 +bug,cli ^2026-10-12T00:42 #01a12d8f-6eeb-74f2-9a4b-ffad237e4126
[ ] Accept a relative path in add action -f =add-file-relative $From clearhead-core, `clearhead add action X -f .clearhead/charters/next.actions` fails with 'Invalid path' while the absolute path works; an absolute path into another workspace (crates/clearhead-cli/.clearhead from clearhead-core) fails the same way. The cause looks like resolve in filesystem/mod.rs (~line 710) stripping the current workspace root before WorkspacePath::new. Resolve -f against the current directory, then find the workspace that owns it. Done when CLI tests add through a relative -f and through an absolute -f into another workspace.$ !3 ^2026-11-25T07:09 #01a2118a-02ee-77b0-9a67-2d01ef22b61e
